  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_lasher",
      "name": {
        "en": "Sand Reckoner's Badge",
        "zh": "衡沙证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_lasher",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Sand Reckoner has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude in combat through control of Clockwork Fowlbeasts.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Supporter Operator during field operations to exercise Summoner responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员衡沙擅长操控发条羽兽参加作战\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为辅助干员，行使召唤师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_lasher",
      "name": {
        "en": "Traces From the Past",
        "zh": "过往留痕",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_lasher",
      "description": {
        "en": "Lazvar opens the heavy door that has shielded him from people's hostility for more than a decade. Absentmindedly, he grabs the beast teaser hanging behind the door and makes a few flicks towards the inside of the room.\nOne, two, three.\nThe newly-engraved gemstone on the tip of the teaser glows faintly, flickering against the darkness, yet the familiar figure doesn't appear as expected. Lazvar stops. It suddenly dawns on him that Mio is never going to magically emerge from nowhere and rush towards him again. Sighing deeply, he hangs the teaser back.\n'Click.' With a faint mechanical sound, soft light illuminates the depths of the room. Priceless gems, coveted even in Menat-Ha'mait, flood the bookshelves and desks, casting vibrant, colorful reflections. In this most secure and secretive room of the Grand Bazaar, they have silently painted an ethereal illusion.\nThese are the fruits of many years of hard work by Lazvar's family. To protect them from bandits and thieves, Lazvar has memorized the precise position of every brick in these four walls, even noting how they're covered by dust.\nBut none of that matters now, for he is finally going to put his long-carried mission aside and leave this place that has begun to paralyze his mind.\nBefore going, Lazvar needs to pack the most important things first. Wait, what are those things on the list again?\nOh yes, the portrait of Mio, Woof and him from a couple of years ago... Here, right behind the shelf. They persuaded him into getting one as a commemoration of coming-of-age, but after the portrait was completed, Woof insisted on hiding it here, claiming, 'Who has ever seen any beckbeast and cloudbeast as large as us!' Mio was so offended that they refused to eat for two days.\nThat old scratching board of Mio is still under the desk! Actually, it was originally a gemstone pillow they gave him when he was little; after Lazvar fell asleep, Mio would curl up next to his head. Later, the pillow became Mio's scratching board, and so Lazvar wrapped it in a brand-new blanket for them to use.\nOf course, there's also this teasing stick behind the door, which was originally a retractable rod gifted by Woof. It used to have a clockwork fowlbeast attached to it. Mio liked to carry this rod in her mouth, and they would chase each other around the house...\nOther than those things, there's only this pile of gemstones sitting here, their beauty now meaningless to him.\nLazvar takes out a broken clockwork fowlbeast—a prop Mio once used countless times at his bedside to perform their trick of 'swallowing a toy and throwing it up whole again', just to make him laugh. The badly-scratched clockwork fowlbeast now lies quietly in his palm, though. It seems Mio has grown out of these kinds of tricks too.\nLazvar clears the carbon box of exquisite gemstones and refills it with his few cherished memories. After some tugging and bumping, everything falls back into silence.\n'Stop watching. We should leave too.'\nA voice softly rings from a dark corner of the room once Lazvar seems to have gone far enough away.",
        "zh": "拉恕尔打开了那扇帮他挡住了十几年恶意的厚重房门，习惯性地抓起了挂在门后的逗宠棒，朝着黑暗的房间深处摇了摇。\n一下，两下，三下。\n刚刚装上去的宝石在黑暗中发出了一连串微弱的亮光，熟悉的身影却没有出现。拉恕尔的手僵在了空气中，他突然想起，米奥不会再像往常一样从角落里冲出来了。他长叹一口气，缓缓地将逗宠棒挂回了门后。\n“啪”，伴随着轻微的机关声，柔和的光线照亮了房间深处的黑暗，那些在米纳特哈玛仪也千金难买的宝石堆满了书架、书桌，它们折射出绚烂多彩的光，在这个大巴扎最安全、最隐秘的房间里无声地勾绘出缥缈的幻景。\n这些都是拉恕尔的家族这么多年来奋斗的“结果”，为了这些宝石不被图谋不轨的人窃取，这个房间每一块砖、每一处灰尘的情况他都了如指掌。\n不过，这都不重要了，拉恕尔所背负的使命已经可以放下了，他要离开这个让他麻木的地方。\n在那之前，他得把自己最重要的一切带走。所以，自己要带走什么来着？\n哦对了，几年前的自己和米奥沃奥的画像，在架子的后面！当时它们执意要带着自己留个成年的纪念，但在画像完成之后，沃奥执意要把画像藏在这里，理由是“谁见过这么大的循兽和云兽啊！”，气得米奥两天没吃饭。\n这个给米奥用过的抓板，在桌子下面！这是小时候米奥给自己准备的宝石枕头，睡着后米奥就趴在自己的头边，后来枕头变成了米奥的抓板，为此自己还给枕头包上了全新的毯子。\n当然，还有这根门后的逗宠棒，最早是沃奥送给自己的伸缩棍，上面原来绑着一个发条羽兽，米奥常常叼着这根棍子和年少的自己在屋子里飞奔追逐……\n除此之外，只剩下这堆对自己没什么意义的宝石。\n拉恕尔从怀里摸出了已经坏掉的发条羽兽，这是米奥无数次在床头通过表演“没有任何损伤地吞下再吐出玩具”来逗得他哈哈大笑的那个道具。但如今，表面布满抓痕的发条羽兽一动不动地躺在他的手心，看来米奥也不想继续表演这种把戏了。\n拉恕尔将华贵的宝石从纸箱中倒出，把他仅有的私人回忆放入其中。在箱子拖曳和房门碰撞的声音消散后，一切又回归了沉寂。\n“别看了，走吧。”\n在脚步声远去后，一个声音在黑暗的房间角落响起。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
